      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "We should be clear that our policy prioritizes the rights of marginalized groups and the stability of the workplace. If a statement, even if not technically hate speech, creates a hostile environment or makes employees feel uncomfortable, it's likely to be considered a problem. We can't stay neutral on this issue, as the very existence of marginalized groups demands that we acknowledge and address the power dynamics at play. By allowing \"uncomfortable\" statements that center on identities, we're implicitly condoning a culture of privilege and silencing marginalized voices. Our policy should explicitly state that we value the safety and well-being of all employees, particularly those from underrepresented groups, and that we will not tolerate language that undermines their dignity or creates a hostile work environment.",
